# This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites text
# files to CRLF in the working copy. Two things must not be rewritten.

# Shell scripts. A CRLF `#!/usr/bin/env bash` line makes the kernel look for an
# interpreter named "bash\r", and the release runner fails with `bad interpreter`
# naming env, which exists, rather than the carriage return, which is the problem.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The console's source, and the build committed beside it. A production build is
# a function of the source bytes, and carriage returns are bytes:
# @vitejs/plugin-vue hashes each component's raw source into its style scope id,
# and vite copies index.html and public/ into the output with their line endings.
# So a CRLF checkout built a different console from CI's Linux one, and CI, which
# fails if the committed console differs from a fresh build, rejected it. LF for
# every text file here makes a Windows build byte-identical; text=auto leaves
# images alone. The output is pinned too, so the bytes a Windows `go build`
# embeds are the committed ones.
ui/** text=auto eol=lf
internal/webui/public/** text=auto eol=lf
